<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69100" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυκτήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύσσομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nostril</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλέγει δὲ μ.</span>, of the fire-breathing
			bull of Aeetes, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				336
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1488
			</span></i>, etc.: freq. in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυκτῆρσιν ἐρευνᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					101
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i>Acut.(Sp.</i>)<i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				893
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				5.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				217.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.249
			</span></i>, al.: dat. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυκτήρεσσιν</span>,
			in a prescription, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1088.32
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>: metaph., of a lamp-<i>nozzle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> from the use
			of the nose to express ridicule, <i>sneerer</i>, of Socrates, Timo
				<i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>; in the abstract, <i>sarcasm, raillery</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. πολιτικώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longin.
					34.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.860e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. Ἀττικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Prom.Es</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεράσας μυκτῆρι φρόνημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.188
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> an elephant's
				<i>trunk</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				497b26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				659a12
			</span></i>; also, the <i>funnel</i> of the cuttlefish, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				541b15
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
